  "limitations": [
    "Exact field ID matching is intentionally strict; registration_number versus registration_num is an example of a semantic alias counted as mismatch. No post-hoc alias adjudication was applied.",
    "Every runtime OCR page set differs from its frozen gold page set. Gold evidence validity and typed-value exact match cannot be read as independent OCR-normalized scores.",
    "Exact spans to the runtime OCR prove traceability to text, not that the selected field or value is semantically correct.",
    "No candidate array[object] field, linked cell, or complete row was proposed despite 429 gold cells and 111 gold rows.",
    "Two public PDFs yielded no OCR text; one exceeded the configured auto-mode length limit and received no model call.",
    "Twelve hash-selected documents are a bounded diagnostic, not an accuracy or cost estimate for arbitrary documents."
  ],
  "decision": "Do not promote this prompt repair to production or launch a 2,000-source Qwen extraction gate. Prioritize OCR robustness and stable source-text provenance, then test canonical field mapping and a table-aware model/parser on pinned held-out documents. Require nonzero linked-row recall and materially better grounded typed-value accuracy before broader inference."
